summary:
I now have the complete picture. Here is the full owner-creation flow.

## Overview of request path

`POST /api/owners` → `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)`. The route is defined on the generated interface `OwnersApi` (path constant `PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners"`, method POST), and the controller class is mapped at `/api`, so the effective path is `/api/owners`. The V2 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) only implements a paged GET list; it has no create endpoint.

Active profile is `spring-data-jpa` + `h2` (`src/main/resources/application.properties:20`), so the repository `save` is Spring Data JPA's default (plain `persist`/`merge`, no custom implementation).

---

## 1. The controller method (the create endpoint)

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:102-189`

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    String normalizedAddress = normalizeAddress(owner.getAddress());
    if (normalizedAddress.isEmpty()) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,
            "Address must not be blank after normalization");
    }
    owner.setAddress(normalizedAddress);
    String normalizedTelephone = normalizeTelephone(owner.getTelephone());
    owner.setTelephone(normalizedTelephone);
    owner.setEmail(normalizeEmail(owner.getEmail()));
    validateEmailDomain(owner.getEmail());
    validatePostcode(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity());
    java.time.LocalDate serverDate = java.time.LocalDate.now();
    if (owner.getRegistrationDate() != null && owner.getRegistrationDate().isAfter(serverDate)) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,
            "Registration date must not be later than the current server date");
    }
    java.time.LocalDate effectiveDate = owner.getRegistrationDate() != null
        ? owner.getRegistrationDate() : serverDate;
    java.time.LocalDate businessDate = toBusinessDay(effectiveDate);
    owner.setRegistrationDate(businessDate);
    long createdToday = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
        .map(Owner::getRegistrationDate)
        .filter(businessDate::equals)
        .count();
    if (createdToday >= 100) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS,
            "The maximum number of owners for today has already been reached");
    }
    owner.setBulkSignupWarning(createdToday > 80);
    String lastNameKey = normalizeForHousehold(owner.getLastName());
    String householdId = householdId(lastNameKey, owner.getPostcode());
    owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
    List<Owner> householdMembers = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
        .filter(existing -> householdId.equals(
            householdId(normalizeForHousehold(existing.getLastName()), existing.getPostcode())))
        .toList();
    String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
    boolean identityInUse = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
        .anyMatch(existing -> identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey()));
    if (identityInUse) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
            "An owner with this identity already exists");
    }
    boolean declaredHouseholdMember = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
    if (!householdMembers.isEmpty() && !declaredHouseholdMember) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
            "An owner in this household already exists");
    }
    String cityKey = normalizeForHousehold(owner.getCity());
    long cityCount = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
        .filter(existing -> normalizeForHousehold(existing.getCity()).equals(cityKey))
        .count();
    if (cityCount >= 50) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
            "This city already has the maximum number of owners");
    }
    owner.setNamesakeCount(namesakeCount(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
    owner.setHouseholdSize(householdMembers.size() + 1);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicate(false);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(null);
    owner.setCustomerCode(customerCode(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode(),
        owner.getTelephone(), owner.getLastName()));
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    AUDIT.info("Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), ownerDto.getMembershipLevel());
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

Note: `addOwner` itself is **not** `@Transactional` (only `deleteOwner` is). Each `clinicService` call runs in its own transaction. The private helper methods it calls (all in the same file) are:
- `normalizeAddress` (`:286`) — trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST/RD/AVE`.
- `normalizeTelephone` (`:375`) + `validateNationalNumberLength` (`:406`) — forces E.164, enforces per-country national digit length (`+61`→9, `+1`→10). 400 on failure.
- `normalizeEmail` (`:475`) — lower-cases.
- `validateEmailDomain` (`:495`) — rejects disposable domains `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`. 400 on failure.
- `validatePostcode` (`:451`) — region range check (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099). 400 on failure.
- `toBusinessDay` (`:201`) — rolls Sat/Sun forward to Monday.
- `householdId` (`:331`) — SHA-256 of `lastNameKey + "|" + postcode`, first 12 hex chars.
- `namesakeCount` (`:218`), `customerCode` (`:243`) + `sha256UpperHex` (`:259`), `normalizeForHousehold` (`:313`).

The `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS`, `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES`, `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` constants are at `:353`, `:433`, `:483`.

### Order of validations / side-effects in the create path
1. Bean Validation on the request body (`@Valid` on the DTO — see section 5) runs **before** the method body.
2. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` maps fields (id and pets ignored).
3. Address normalized; 400 if blank after normalization.
4. Telephone normalized to E.164 + national-length check (400).
5. Email lower-cased; disposable-domain check (400).
6. Postcode region-range check (400).
7. Future registration date rejected (400); else defaulted to server date, rolled to business day.
8. **Rate limit**: ≥100 owners already registered for that business date → 429.
9. `bulkSignupWarning` set when >80 today.
10. `householdId` computed and set.
11. **Identity duplicate**: whole `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) already in use → 409.
12. **Household duplicate**: any existing household member and `sharesHousehold != true` → 409.
13. **City cap**: ≥50 owners in the same city → 409.
14. Sets `namesakeCount`, `householdSize`, `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`, `customerCode`.
15. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` persists.
16. Maps to DTO, writes an **AUDIT log line**, sets `Location` header, returns 201.

Every duplicate/limit check calls `clinicService.findAllOwners()` (a full table scan), repeatedly.

---

## 2. The Owner entity and its Bean Validation annotations

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java:36-88` (field/annotation portion):

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "owners")
public class Owner extends Person {
    @Column(name = "address")
    @NotEmpty
    private String address;

    @Column(name = "city")
    @NotEmpty
    private String city;

    @Column(name = "postcode")
    private String postcode;

    @Column(name = "telephone")
    @NotEmpty
    @Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "Telephone must be in E.164 format (a '+' followed by 8 to 15 digits)")
    private String telephone;

    @Column(name = "email")
    @Email
    private String email;

    @Column(name = "registration_date")
    private LocalDate registrationDate;

    @Column(name = "birth_date")
    private LocalDate birthDate;

    @Column(name = "customer_code")   private String customerCode;
    @Column(name = "household_id")    private String householdId;
    @Column(name = "namesake_count")  private Integer namesakeCount;
    @Column(name = "bulk_signup_warning") private Boolean bulkSignupWarning;
    @Column(name = "household_size")  private Integer householdSize;
    @Column(name = "possible_duplicate") private Boolean possibleDuplicate;
    @Column(name = "possible_duplicate_of") private Integer possibleDuplicateOf;

    @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
    private Set<Pet> pets;
```

Entity-level Bean Validation constraints: `@NotEmpty` on `address`, `city`, `telephone`; `@Pattern` E.164 on `telephone`; `@Email` on `email`. These are enforced by Hibernate's `BeanValidationEventListener` on flush/persist (validation-mode AUTO), i.e. at `saveOwner` time, in addition to the DTO-level validation.

Parent class `Person` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java:28-53`) contributes:
```java
@MappedSuperclass
public class Person extends BaseEntity {
    @Column(name = "first_name") @NotEmpty protected String firstName;
    @Column(name = "last_name")  @NotEmpty protected String lastName;
    ...
}
```

`BaseEntity` (`.../model/BaseEntity.java:31-48`) supplies the `@Id @GeneratedValue(IDENTITY)` id and `isNew()` (`id == null`) — this decides insert vs update in the repository. No lifecycle callbacks here.

`Owner` also has derived/transient helpers used during creation and DTO mapping: `getIdentityKey()` (`@Transient`, `:342`), `getCheckDigit()` (`@Transient`, `:356`), `getTelephoneDisplay()` (`@Transient`, `:138`), and the static scoring methods `ageBandOf` (`:200`), `tenureExceedsOneYear` (`:225`), `membershipPoints` (`:240`), `membershipLevel` (`:264`). The `pets` collection cascades `ALL` but is ignored by the create mapper, so no pets are persisted on owner create.

---

## 3. Service-layer methods used during creation

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {   // line 234
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}

@Override
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public Collection<Owner> findAllOwners() throws DataAccessException {   // line 127
    return ownerRepository.findAll();
}
```

`saveOwner` is `@Transactional` (read-write); `findAllOwners` is `@Transactional(readOnly = true)`. Both are thin pass-throughs to the repository — no additional validation, events, or side effects in the service layer. (`addOwner` calls `findAllOwners` multiple times and `saveOwner` once.) Interface declared in `ClinicService.java`.

---

## 4. Repository methods used

Interface `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`:
- `void save(Owner owner)` (`:66`)
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()` (`:74`)

Active implementation (profile `spring-data-jpa`): `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java:37` — extends `OwnerRepository` and Spring Data `Repository<Owner, Integer>`. It only overrides the `findByLastName`/`findById`/paged `findAll` queries; `save(Owner)` and no-arg `findAll()` fall through to Spring Data's default CRUD implementation (`SimpleJpaRepository` → `persist` for new entity since `isNew()` is true, else `merge`). No custom save logic, no hooks. (Alternate impls `jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` and `jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` exist but are inactive under the current profile.)

